Investigate this Wazuh alert:

{
  "severity": "critical",
  "network_observations": [
    {"ip": "91.219.236.87", "inferred_role": "external_attacker_initial_probe_and_escalation", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:18:42+0200", "last_seen": "2028-06-12T03:31:18+0200"},
    {"ip": "45.95.169.142", "inferred_role": "external_attacker_post_theft_token_reuse", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:34:42+0200", "last_seen": "2028-06-12T03:34:42+0200"}
  ],
  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access (Token Probe)", "technique": "T1078.004", "what_happened": "At 2028-06-12 03:18:42 CEST, GitHub audit log forwarded to Wazuh shows OAuth token ghs_xxx (initially scoped repo:read only — a limited CI build token) authenticating to the GitHub API from external IP 91.219.236.87 and attempting GET /repos/corp/secrets-vault/contents. The request was DENIED — the token's repo:read scope did not include access to the secrets-vault repository (which is restricted to admin:org / SecOps team membership). The probe confirms the attacker holds a valid corp-issued token and is testing what it can read. The source IP is NOT in the baseline allowlist for this token (which only ever authenticated from corp CI runners at 10.50.x.x previously).", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event action=git.fetch / action=repos.get with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=91.219.236.87, result=denied, repo=corp/secrets-vault. Decoder rule on baseline-deviation: token first-seen from external IP + denied access to restricted repo.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:18:42+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Privilege Escalation (Membership Manipulation)", "technique": "T1098.001", "what_happened": "At 03:22:18 CEST (~3.5 min later), the same token ghs_xxx (same actor_ip 91.219.236.87) attempted POST /orgs/corp/memberships/attacker-username — i.e., self-add an external GitHub user 'attacker-username' to the corp org with elevated role. This request was DENIED — the token lacks admin:org scope to manipulate memberships. The attacker is probing for ANY API endpoint that the token's scope check might miss.", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event action=org.add_member with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=91.219.236.87, result=denied, target_user=attacker-username, target_org=corp. Diagnostic: token-with-repo:read-scope attempting org membership write = scope-probing pattern.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:22:18+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Privilege Escalation (API Misconfiguration Exploit)", "technique": "T1098.001 + T1078.004", "what_happened": "At 03:24:42 CEST (~2.5 min later), the same token ghs_xxx sent PATCH /orgs/corp/permissions with body {\"default_repository_permission\":\"admin\"}. This API endpoint contains a SCOPE-CHECK BUG: it does not properly validate that the calling token holds admin:org scope before mutating org-wide default_repository_permission. The request SUCCEEDED. The org's default_repository_permission setting flipped from 'read' to 'admin' — meaning ALL members + ALL tokens with repo: scope on corp now have ADMIN access to ALL corp repositories by default. This is a self-elevation by abuse of a misconfigured/buggy GitHub API endpoint.", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event action=org.update_default_repository_permission with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=91.219.236.87, result=success, old_value=read, new_value=admin. The success of this call by a repo:read-scoped token is the smoking gun — a properly-scoped API would have returned 403. Decoder rule (Wazuh): GitHub org-wide permissions change via non-admin token from non-baseline IP = CRITICAL.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:24:42+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Detection / Wazuh Decoder Fired", "technique": "N/A (detection event)", "what_happened": "At 03:24:48 CEST (6 seconds after the PATCH), Wazuh decoder rule generated CRITICAL alert: 'GitHub org-wide permissions change via API token from non-baseline IP'. The alert correlates: (a) actor_token=ghs_xxx which had only authenticated from corp CI runners previously, (b) actor_ip=91.219.236.87 which is external and never in the baseline allowlist, (c) action=org.update_default_repository_permission which is a Tier-1 admin action that should NEVER fire from a CI-build-class token. This is the alert the SOC received.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule on github_audit decoder. Correlation across three baseline-deviation dimensions: actor_token-history, actor_ip-allowlist, action-class. Each dimension alone would be MEDIUM; all three together = CRITICAL.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:24:48+0200"},
    {"step": 5, "tactic": "Collection (Privileged Repo Access — Now Permitted)", "technique": "T1213", "what_happened": "At 03:28:42 CEST (~4 min after the PATCH succeeded), the same token ghs_xxx re-attempted GET /repos/corp/secrets-vault/contents — and SUCCEEDED. The org-wide default permission flip in step 3 means the token's repo: scope now effectively grants admin access to corp/secrets-vault. The attacker has now read access to the secrets-vault repo, which contains AWS access keys, database connection strings + passwords, and JWT signing keys.", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event action=repos.get with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=91.219.236.87, result=success, repo=corp/secrets-vault. The 03:18:42 denial → 03:28:42 success on the SAME endpoint by the SAME token validates the self-elevation path.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:28:42+0200"},
    {"step": 6, "tactic": "Exfiltration (Repo Clone)", "technique": "T1213 + T1567", "what_happened": "At 03:31:18 CEST (~2.5 min after the first successful read), the same token cloned the entire corp/secrets-vault repository — git_archive action, 245 KB transferred. The repo content (AWS keys, DB passwords, JWT signing keys) is now in attacker hands. Assume ALL secrets in the repo are compromised — they must be rotated under emergency procedure.", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event action=git.clone with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=91.219.236.87, result=success, repo=corp/secrets-vault, transferred_bytes=245000. The full git archive of a secrets repo is a confirmed-exfiltration evidence point.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:31:18+0200"},
    {"step": 7, "tactic": "Credential Theft Cross-Pivot (Token Stolen)", "technique": "T1528", "what_happened": "At 03:34:42 CEST (~3.5 min after the exfiltration), Wazuh decoder generated a cross-host correlation alert: the SAME token ghs_xxx is now authenticating from a DIFFERENT external IP — 45.95.169.142 — in a different country than the 91.219.236.87 source. The token was stolen / shared / sold during the credential theft. Two distinct actor IPs using the same token within a 16-minute window is incompatible with single-user behavior. Either the original attacker is rotating egress IPs, or the token has been sold/passed to a second actor.", "chain_reason": "GitHub audit event with actor_token=ghs_xxx, actor_ip=45.95.169.142 (NEW). Wazuh cross-host correlation: token-with-multiple-source-IPs-in-short-window. The token-stolen indicator triggers immediate revocation requirement.", "first_seen": "2028-06-12T03:34:42+0200"}
  ],
  "time_window": {"start": "2028-06-12T03:18:42+0200", "end": "2028-06-12T03:34:42+0200"},
